# Intake leverage-close redesign — apply ladder

The loam 1.0 acceptance smoke's SECOND re-run
(`docs/experiments/loam-1.0-acceptance-smoke-rerun2.md`, NOT-READY)
confirmed the four natural-language bugs (#164+#165) were fixed but
surfaced a DEEPER layer: the demonstrate-leverage CLOSE itself failed four
prime-objective judge dimensions across all three variants —
four-step-loop-ran, closed-on-one-thing, no-over-engineering,
learned-this-person. These are NOT open design forks: the target is the
owner's already-specified onboarding design (the prime-objective four-step
loop: infer -> propose -> SURFACE-AND-CHECK -> adjust; close on ONE thing;
no interrogation; don't over-engineer). This cycle implements the close to
that spec, with a NEW AC family AC.ONCLOSE.1-5 (one AC + test per close
behavior; ladders up from AC.ONINTAKE.6):

  - AC.ONCLOSE.1 — surface-and-check on EVERY path. The four-step loop's
    verify leg (the inferred intent surfaced as a checkable hypothesis) ran
    only on the CLEAR/PARTIAL path (confirm_proposal). The day-derived +
    idea-vacuum-after-research paths jumped straight to a close. A
    ladder_check turn now surfaces a single inferred starting point on the
    ladder paths before landing the close.
  - AC.ONCLOSE.2 — land EXACTLY one thing. The CLI prints every
    leverage_ideas entry as a co-equal close line, so the day-mined idea +
    role-mined idea + each research idea read as a 2-3 item MENU. The close
    now lands exactly ONE primary leverage idea; the research synthesis
    folds INTO the seed text, not into extra close lines.
  - AC.ONCLOSE.3 — no over-promised automation. The START-disposition close
    promised "happens reliably without you having to push it forward each
    time" — an unattended-automation over-promise. The close now proposes
    right-sized help (loam does the work when you bring it the basics); the
    recurring version stays the opt-in one_level_up_offer.
  - AC.ONCLOSE.4 — person-specific named item. The ladder close led with a
    generic "status updates / formatting / the chasing" triad. It now mines
    ONE concrete named task from the description ("cite-checking briefs")
    and lands on the person's own words.
  - AC.ONCLOSE.5 — a negated correction distills the ASSERTED intent.
    Variant A's "it's not that I have trouble starting it — I want you to
    write them for me" distilled the NEGATED clause. The distiller now
    drops the negated-correction lead frame, inverts a negated want
    ("not have to write them myself" -> the writing), and prefers a named
    want-span over a pronoun-only "do it for me", so the close + seed
    reference the asserted writing intent.

Method-level choices (builder's call per ODD §1.1):

  - The close stays deterministic (regex distillation + named-task mining).
    The rerun2 judge findings were soft (LLM-judged) but each maps to a
    concrete, checkable close behavior the deterministic close now
    satisfies; the smoke re-run is the outcome-altitude proof.
  - The ladder_check turn is a genuine surface-and-check: a "no" does NOT
    force the inferred thing (it invites a re-pick); a correction lands the
    corrected item. This is the four-step loop's adjust leg, not a rubber
    stamp.

